  "raw_text": "14\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb81\n):\n \nÂimplikra kum lalahkam implikaia sip sa, kuna Jehova wal pâna lâka brisma ba upla kumi sin implikbia apia\n \n–\n \nA\nthief can steal your money, but no one will steal the friendship you have with Jehovah\n \n/ Un ladrón puede robar tu dinero, pero\nnadie robará la amistad que tienes con Jehová)\n\nAikabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto vomit\n \n/ vomitar\n\nAikabaia munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cause to vomit\n \n/ hacer vomitar\n\nAikaia\n \n(v-irregularity of / irregularidad de:\n \nYabaia\n \n–\n \nto give\n \n/ dar; See also/ Ver también:\n \nMaikaia\n \n&\n \nWankaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto give\nme, to allow me, to cause me\n \n/ darme, permitirme, hacerme\n\n(Ex/Ej-Present tense/Tiempo presente:\n \nYang aikisna\n \n–\n \nI give myself\n \n/ Me doy;\n \nMan aikisma\n \n–\n \nYou give me\n \n/ Me das;\n \nWitin aikisa\n \n–\n\nHe/she gives me\n \n/ El/ella me da)\n\n(Ex/Ej-Past tense/Tiempo pasado:\n \nYang aikri\n \n–\n \nI gave myself\n \n/ Me di;\n \nMan aikram\n \n–\n \nYou gave me\n \n/ Me diste;\n \nWitin aikan\n \n–\n \nHe/she\ngave me\n \n/ El/ella me dio)\n\n(Ex/Ej- Future tense/Tiempo futuro:\n \nYang aikamna\n \n–\n \nI will give myself\n \n/ Me daré;\n \nMan aikma\n \n–\n \nYou will give me\n \n/ Me darás;\n \nWitin\naikbia\n \n–\n \nHe/she will give me\n \n/ El/ella me dará)\n\nAik\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \ngive me, allow me, let me\n \n/ dame, permíteme, déjeme\n\nSal aik\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \nget it and give it to me\n \n/ consíguelo y dámelo\n\nWira aik\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \ngive me a little please\n \n/ dame un poco por favor\n\nAikrika\n \n(v-imp-alt)\n \n–\n \nallow me, let me\n \n/ permíteme, déjeme\n\n(Ex/Ej\n:\n \nAikrika wamna\n \n–\n \nPermit me to go\n \n/ Permíteme ir)\n\nAikarbaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nAikarwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto roll up, to wallow, to roll\n \n/ enrollarse, revolcarse, rodar\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \ndict\n \nsays\n \nAikarbaia\n \nis intransitive but this seems to be a mistake /\n \ndict\n \ndice que\n \nAikarbaia\n \nes intransitiva pero esto\nparece ser un error)\n\nAikarwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nAikarbaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto roll up, to wallow, to roll\n \n/ enrollarse, revolcarse, rodar\n\nAiklabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto fight, to battle, to struggle, to debate, to contend\n \n/ luchar, pelear, debatir, contender\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \ndb\n \nuses\n \nAiklas\n \nas the imperative form /\n \ndb\n \nusa\n \nAiklas\n \ncomo la forma imperativa)\n\nAiklabaia daknika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \narmy, battalion, group for fighting\n \n/ ejército, batallón, grupo de batalla\n\nAiklabaia dusa\n \n(\nmy\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \njavelin\n \n/ jabalina\n\nAiklabaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nweapon\n \n/ arma\n\nAiklabanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfight, battle, struggle, debate, contention, war\n \n/ lucha, batalla, debate, contención, guerra\n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nWar aiklabanka\n)\n\nAiklabanka mayunra\n \n(\nmy50\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \npraise for the fight, praise for the battle\n \n/ alabanza por la pelea,\nalabanza por la batalla\n\nWar aiklabanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbattle in a war, war\n \n/\n \nbatalla en una guerra, guerra\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n12/19\n):\n \nG\nâ\nd war\n \naiklabanka ba war nani sut\n \nâ\npu daukbia\n \n–\n \nGod’s war to end all wars\n \n/\n \nL\na guerra de\n\nDios para poner fin a todas las guerras\n)\n\nG\nâ\nd las war aiklabanka tara\n \n–\n \nGod’s great final war\n \n/\n \nL\na gran guerra final de Dios\n\nWar Aiklabanka Kau Tara\n \n–\n \nWorld War 1\n \n/ Primera Guerra Mundial\n \n(Alt:\n \nTasba aiska pas war\naiklabanka\n)\n\nTasba aiska war aiklabanka wala\n \n–\n \nWorld War 2\n \n/ Segunda Guerra Mundial\n\nAiklaklabra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfighter, warrior\n,\n \nsoldier,\n \narmy\n \n/\n \nluchador, guerrero, soldado, ejército\n\n(\nConstruct:\n \nAiklaklabriki\n;\n \nA\niklaklabrikam\n;\n \nAiklaklabrika\n)\n\nAiklaklabra dakni\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \narmy, troops, battalion\n \n/\n \nejército, tropas, batallón\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmy50\n):\n \nAi aiklaklabra daknika\n \n–\n \nhis army\n \n/\n \nsu ej\né\nrcito\n)\n\nMapara aiklaklabra\n \n–\n \nopposing fighter,\n \nopposing warrior\n \n/\n \nluchador\n \ncontrario\n, guerrero opuesto\n\nWar aiklaklabra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nfighter, warrior, army\n \n/\n \nluchador, guerrero, ejército\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nIsa36:1\n):\n \nwar aiklaklabra tara\n \n–\n \nvast army\n \n/\n \ngran ejercito\n)\n\nMapara aiklabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto fight against\n \n/ luchar contra\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nkm10/14\n):\n \nGridi lâka mapara aiklabaia dukiara dîa hilp wan munbia?\n \n–\n \nWhat will help us to fight against greed?\n \n/\n¿Qué nos ayudará a luchar contra la codicia?)\n\nAikrika\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nAikaia\n\nAikuki\n \n–\n \nwith, united, together, in company of, along with, together with\n \n/ con, unidos, juntos, en compañía de, junto\ncon\n \n(See also / Ver también:\n \nKuki\n)\n\nAikuki asla prakan\n \n–\n \nunited together\n \n/ unidos juntos\n\nAikuki balaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto come together\n \n/ venir juntos",
